        "section_equations": "SUSY context; Sections2,3,7 Eqs7.4-7.8; AppendixA EqsA.5-A.9"
      },
      "fact": "The source treats supersymmetric SM extensions. Three ordinary quark generations carry explicitly stated GSM representations. The low-energy regime has two Higgs doublets, singlet scalars S1,S2 (or explicitly replaced by one S), and three light charged-lepton generations after heavy-field removal. Horizontal continuous charges are bookkeeping for a discrete symmetry, not additional local U1 gauge factors."
    },
    {
      "id": "p28-susy",
      "basis": "supersymmetry_representation_derivation",
      "locator": {
        "pdf_pages": [
          2,
          17,
          19,
          28,
          29
        ],
        "section_equations": "Section7 SUSY/holomorphy discussion and AppendixA light spectrum"
      },
      "fact": "In this source SUSY regime, the displayed charged scalar/matter fields belong to chiral multiplets (one complex scalar plus one LH Weyl); GSM vector multiplets supply one adjoint gaugino per factor. The declared MSSM template expands this implication. No auxiliary fields or dependent conjugates count as matter."
    },
    {
      "id": "p28-EFT-not-UV",
      "basis": "source_statement",
      "locator": {
        "pdf_pages": [
          18,
          19,
          20,
          28,
          29
        ],
        "section_equations": "Section7 heavy-quark completion; AppendixA heavy-lepton alternatives"
      },
      "fact": "The heavy quark and heavy charged-lepton fields are integrated out in the selected light EFT. The six-versus-three-heavy-lepton alternatives and heavy quark regimes are not summed into the light inventory. The one-S alternative explicitly replaces, not adds to, S1,S2."
    }
  ],
